abstract: >-
  Spatia is a reproducible, open platform for subnational geospatial
  analysis of northeast Argentina (NEA) and its cross-border regions
  (Paraguay, southern Brazil). It combines satellite imagery (Sentinel-1/2,
  Landsat, MODIS, VIIRS), census data and open geospatial datasets on a
  hexagonal grid (H3 resolution 9), from ~320,000 hexagons for Misiones to
  more than a million for Corrientes and Chaco, across 24 provinces,
  departments and states. Most layers report physical values directly
  (percent of buildings on low ground, tree cover loss rate, PM2.5 in
  ug/m3, travel minutes, census rates); the few composite scores use
  equal-weight geometric means of PCA-selected components. The pipeline
  runs on Google Earth Engine, processes rasters into H3 zonal statistics
  and serves results via DuckDB-WASM on Cloudflare Pages. It offers 15
  analyses across four thematic lenses: environment and risk, production
  and land, population and services, and economy and trade.
